<!--
  Each entry below is a deliberate, reviewed break. Regenerating this file with
  /p:ApiCompatGenerateSuppressionFile=true drops these comments, so re-add them.

  CP0002 x4, Error.NotFound.For / Error.Gone.For (3.0.0-alpha.496):
  a trailing optional `code` parameter was added to all four factories, so the
  two-parameter signatures no longer exist. Source-compatible - every existing
  call site still compiles unchanged - but binary-breaking, so a consumer
  compiled against 3.0.0-alpha.495 must rebuild rather than drop in the new
  assembly.

  Adding the parameter rather than overloading is forced: an overload leading
  with `code` would make the existing `For<T>("some-id")` bind to the new method,
  silently turning an id into a reason code. A signature change fails loudly at
  compile time instead.
-->
